<title>CANADA: United Grain to build C$9.5 mln facility.</title>
<headline>United Grain to build C$9.5 mln facility.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Grain Growers Ltd on Wednesday said it plans to spend C$9.5 million to build a 32,000-tonne high-throughput grain elevator later this year 16 miles east of Calgary, a UGG statement said.</p>
<p>The facility should be operational by the summer of 1998 and will be able to spot 112 hopper cars within 24 hours.</p>
<p>UGG has built 12 high through put elevators since 1993 with this latest investment bringing the total capital expenditures to C$138 million, the statement said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Reuters Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
